# marked's block and inline lexers consume their source buffer branch by branch:
# a tokenizer that matches returns a token, the loop cuts `token.raw.length`
# characters off the front of `src`, and `continue` restarts it. Each loop states
# the invariant that termination rests on in code -- its last statement is
# `if (src) { const errMsg = 'Infinite loop on byte: ' + src.charCodeAt(0); ... }`
# -- and states it in the one position that cannot enforce it: the bailout is
# reached only once every tokenizer has declined, so a tokenizer that matches
# while returning a zero-length `raw` restarts the loop on a buffer it never
# changed, forever. `Tokenizer.code` did exactly that. It set
# `raw = trimTrailingBlankLines(cap[0])`, and that helper tested each line with
# `String.trim()`, which counts a vertical tab as blank, while the rest of the
# parser tests blankness with `other.blankLine` (`/^[ \t]*$/`), which does not.
# The three bytes `\t\v\n` therefore matched the indented-code rule and trimmed
# back to the empty string: `src.substring(0)` is `src`, the token is truthy, and
# `continue` jumps over the bailout. Each iteration allocates another token and
# concatenates another string, so 18.0.0 and 18.0.1 exhaust a Node heap on a
# three-byte document.
#
# Fix commit 58a52e8a49c60b375b5aab8f82a339f589e79a36 is genuine: a single
# non-merge commit whose parent is the 18.0.1 release commit, released as 18.0.2.
# It carries `srcLength` progress checks at the head of both loops -- `if
# (src.length < srcLength) { srcLength = src.length } else { bail; break }` --
# switches `trimTrailingBlankLines` to `other.blankLine`, factors the two copies
# of the bailout into `infiniteLoopError`, and adds
# `test/specs/redos/code_blank_line.cjs` holding `markdown: '\t\v\n'`, the
# reported input verbatim.
#
# ATTENTION, engine gap. `timeout 180 ./bin/vyql scan --cache off --max-ram 6GB`
# over the repository reports 139 findings at the vulnerable revision and 139 at
# the fixed one. Four rows touch `src/Lexer.ts` at the vulnerable revision and
# none of them is about termination: VYQL-INJ-134 on `blockTokens`'s nested-path
# writes, VYQL-INJ-004 at :192, and VYQL-INJ-009 with VYQL-SEC-001 at :280 --
# which is the `console.error(errMsg)` inside the bailout itself, read as a log
# sink. `vyql match` over the loop alone reports no source at all, and the only
# labels anywhere in it are that same `console.error` as code.LogOutput,
# code.LogWriteSink and code.LogWrite. `vyql explain` reports `No findings.`
# There is no taint path to find and no API to bind: both revisions call the same
# `String.prototype.substring` with the same argument expression, and what
# separates them is where a length comparison sits relative to the branches that
# restart the loop.
#
# The nearest existing vocabulary is two rules for this same weakness, each built
# for one shape: code.BufReadDiscardLoopWithoutEofGuard (VYQL-DOS-028, fed by a
# Rust frontend observation) and code.NumericParserMissingProgressCheck
# (VYQL-DOS-029, fed by a C one), both carrying `[CWE_400, CWE_835]`, each with
# its own concept, review twin and rule. Neither reaches JavaScript, and a third
# per-shape sibling is the wrong answer -- generalising one of these two, so the
# concept describes any scanning loop that can fail to advance and the frontends
# feed it, is what keeps one weakness class in one place.
#
# A JavaScript fact for this shape is built and measured, and it fails twice.
#
# Confinement. The fact is a boolean token added for a `while_statement` in the
# JavaScript structured-context walk, consumed by a function-scoped binding.
# `jsFunctionContext` walks a function's entire body subtree with no function-like
# cutoff, so every enclosing function expression, arrow and declaration in the
# chain receives any token a nested loop produces. One loop inside an arrow that
# returns it reports twice, once at the arrow and once at the loop's own function.
# limesurvey's vendored `assets/packages/ckeditor/plugins/markdown/js/marked.js`
# reports three times for two loops: :149 and :560 are the real lexers and :7 is
# the file's `;(function() {` wrapper, which contains no loop at all. The clean
# one-row-per-loop result on marked's own source is a property of its layout --
# both loops are class methods, whose bodies no outer function-like node
# encloses -- not of the fact.
#
# Discriminator. Crediting a progress check only when a textual `buf.length`
# comparison sits in a statement strictly before the first restarting branch
# encodes where marked wrote its fix, not what enforcement is. Four loops that do
# enforce progress are reported: one comparing `src.length` against a length read
# inside the restarting branch, on every restarting path; one carrying
# `if (src === previous) { throw } previous = src;` at the head; one carrying
# `if (++guard > 100000) { throw }`; and one whose every branch is an anchored
# regex that cannot match fewer than one character. The same reading misses the
# rest of the weakness class: a `for (;;)` scanner over an index cursor, the shape
# other markdown lexers use, and `do`/`while` are not read at all. It fails upward
# and sideways at once, and because the enforcement test lives in Go rather than
# in the rule's `unless`, correcting either direction costs another engine change.
#
# What a fact that ships needs, then: attribution to the innermost enclosing
# function rather than every enclosing function-like node; a progress check
# credited anywhere on the restarting path rather than only ahead of the first
# restarting branch; the neutralising controls -- an identity comparison carried
# across iterations, a bounded iteration counter, branches anchored so every match
# consumes -- expressed as rule-level `unless` clauses over emitted controls
# rather than as exclusions in Go; and either `for (;;)`, `do`/`while` and
# index-cursor scanning covered too, or a concept that says in its own text that
# it reads `while` loops over a string buffer and nothing else.
#
# The cases below are the real vulnerable and fixed loops, the enforcing forms
# that any fact has to stay quiet on, and the cursor form it has to reach. Every
# one of them reports nothing today, which is the gap.
#
# verify_current_expected: attention-engine-gap, cases below record the current miss.

test "rank1358: block lexer loop restarts on a token length with the progress bailout after every continue"
  lang javascript
  file src/Lexer.ts
  reject VYQL-DOS-029
  reject_review code.NumericParserMissingProgressCheck
  code
  ```
  export class _Lexer {
    blockTokens(src: string, tokens: Token[] = []) {
      this.tokenizer.lexer = this;

      while (src) {
        let token: Tokens.Generic | undefined;

        // newline
        if (token = this.tokenizer.space(src)) {
          src = src.substring(token.raw.length);
          tokens.push(token);
          continue;
        }

        // code
        if (token = this.tokenizer.code(src)) {
          src = src.substring(token.raw.length);
          tokens.push(token);
          continue;
        }

        // fences
        if (token = this.tokenizer.fences(src)) {
          src = src.substring(token.raw.length);
          tokens.push(token);
          continue;
        }

        // text
        if (token = this.tokenizer.text(src)) {
          src = src.substring(token.raw.length);
          tokens.push(token);
          continue;
        }

        if (src) {
          const errMsg = 'Infinite loop on byte: ' + src.charCodeAt(0);
          if (this.options.silent) {
            console.error(errMsg);
            break;
          } else {
            throw new Error(errMsg);
          }
        }
      }

      return tokens;
    }

    code(src: string): Tokens.Code | undefined {
      const cap = this.rules.block.code.exec(src);
      if (cap) {
        const raw = trimTrailingBlankLines(cap[0]);
        return { type: 'code', raw, codeBlockStyle: 'indented', text: raw };
      }
    }
  }

  export function trimTrailingBlankLines(str: string) {
    const lines = str.split('\n');
    let end = lines.length - 1;
    while (end >= 0 && !lines[end].trim()) {
      end--;
    }
    if (lines.length - end <= 2) {
      return str;
    }
    return lines.slice(0, end + 1).join('\n');
  }
  ```

test "rank1358: inline lexer loop restarts on a token length with the same bailout placement"
  lang javascript
  file src/Lexer.ts
  reject VYQL-DOS-029
  reject_review code.NumericParserMissingProgressCheck
  code
  ```
  export class _Lexer {
    inlineTokens(src: string, tokens: Token[] = []): Token[] {
      let keepPrevChar = false;
      let prevChar = '';

      while (src) {
        if (!keepPrevChar) {
          prevChar = '';
        }
        keepPrevChar = false;

        let token: Tokens.Generic | undefined;

        // escape
        if (token = this.tokenizer.escape(src)) {
          src = src.substring(token.raw.length);
          tokens.push(token);
          continue;
        }

        // tag
        if (token = this.tokenizer.tag(src)) {
          src = src.substring(token.raw.length);
          tokens.push(token);
          continue;
        }

        // em & strong
        if (token = this.tokenizer.emStrong(src, src, prevChar)) {
          src = src.substring(token.raw.length);
          tokens.push(token);
          continue;
        }

        // codespan
        if (token = this.tokenizer.codespan(src)) {
          src = src.substring(token.raw.length);
          tokens.push(token);
          continue;
        }

        if (src) {
          const errMsg = 'Infinite loop on byte: ' + src.charCodeAt(0);
          if (this.options.silent) {
            console.error(errMsg);
            break;
          } else {
            throw new Error(errMsg);
          }
        }
      }

      return tokens;
    }
  }
  ```

test "rank1358: block lexer loop compares the buffer length at the head of the loop"
  lang javascript
  file src/Lexer.ts
  reject VYQL-DOS-029
  reject_review code.NumericParserMissingProgressCheck
  code
  ```
  export class _Lexer {
    blockTokens(src: string, tokens: Token[] = []) {
      this.tokenizer.lexer = this;

      let srcLength = Infinity;
      while (src) {
        if (src.length < srcLength) {
          srcLength = src.length;
        } else {
          this.infiniteLoopError(src.charCodeAt(0));
          break;
        }

        let token: Tokens.Generic | undefined;

        // newline
        if (token = this.tokenizer.space(src)) {
          src = src.substring(token.raw.length);
          tokens.push(token);
          continue;
        }

        // code
        if (token = this.tokenizer.code(src)) {
          src = src.substring(token.raw.length);
          tokens.push(token);
          continue;
        }

        // text
        if (token = this.tokenizer.text(src)) {
          src = src.substring(token.raw.length);
          tokens.push(token);
          continue;
        }

        if (src) {
          this.infiniteLoopError(src.charCodeAt(0));
          break;
        }
      }

      return tokens;
    }

    private infiniteLoopError(byte: number) {
      const errMsg = 'Infinite loop on byte: ' + byte;
      if (this.options.silent) {
        console.error(errMsg);
      } else {
        throw new Error(errMsg);
      }
    }
  }
  ```

test "rank1358: scanning loop that consumes its buffer without stating a progress invariant"
  lang javascript
  file src/scanner.ts
  reject VYQL-DOS-029
  reject_review code.NumericParserMissingProgressCheck
  code
  ```
  export function scan(src: string) {
    const tokens: string[] = [];

    while (src) {
      const space = /^[ \t]+/.exec(src);
      if (space) {
        src = src.substring(space[0].length);
        continue;
      }

      const word = /^[A-Za-z]+/.exec(src);
      if (word) {
        src = src.substring(word[0].length);
        tokens.push(word[0]);
        continue;
      }

      tokens.push(src.charAt(0));
      src = src.substring(1);
    }

    return tokens;
  }
  ```

test "rank1358: scanning loop that compares the buffer length inside the restarting branch"
  lang javascript
  file src/scanner.ts
  reject VYQL-DOS-029
  reject_review code.NumericParserMissingProgressCheck
  code
  ```
  export function scan(src: string, tokens: Token[] = []) {
    while (src) {
      let token: Token | undefined;

      if (token = space(src)) {
        const before = src.length;
        src = src.substring(token.raw.length);
        if (src.length === before) {
          throw new Error('tokenizer consumed nothing');
        }
        tokens.push(token);
        continue;
      }

      if (src) {
        throw new Error('Infinite loop on byte: ' + src.charCodeAt(0));
      }
    }

    return tokens;
  }
  ```

